Regulator vendors no third-party source. Every dependency is resolved from its
upstream package index at build time and none of it is copied into this tree.
The control-plane skeleton (credential encryption at rest, the signed session
cookie, the Portainer deploy script) follows the shape of the sibling project
Stoker (https://github.com/livehybrid/stoker, Apache-2.0, same author); what
was adapted from it is recorded in docs/VENDOR-FROM-STOKER.md.

The container images redistribute open-source dependencies under their own
licences: httpx, h2, PyYAML, FastAPI, Starlette, uvicorn, SQLAlchemy, pydantic,
cryptography and itsdangerous (all BSD or MIT), and the browser image is built
on Microsoft's Playwright image, which carries Chromium under the BSD licence.
